01
Site: Prairie Corridor Business Park PV (PXA-2024-0343), 2200 Corridor Parkway, Halston, Alleron 05HA.
Issued under TCS-02 §3.1 for the customer-furnished items and the utility installation. Construction package
reference: Prairie Corridor POI civil and electrical package, Rev 2.
1. Location
RTU enclosure mounted on the utility equipment pad beside the POI recloser pad, on the utility side of the point
of interconnection, with 24-hour crew access from Corridor Parkway (DPS-07 §4.2 item 6 for the recloser pad).
2. Bill of materials
Item Description Furnished by
1 RTU, Kelvraith YOT-8963 (TCS-02 §3.2), tag PC-RTU-01 Alleniom Utilities
2 Enclosure, NEMA 4X stainless, 36 x 30 x 12 in, with thermostatic Customer
heater; locked and tamper-evident, Alleniom lock core, keys held by
Alleniom; door switch wired to RTU digital input DI 1 (TCS-02 §7.6)
3 Station service: dedicated 20 A, 120 V branch circuit from panel LP-2, Customer
circuit 14, through a 1.5 kVA online UPS, Corvane OL-1500R, rated 4.5
h at the RTU load (TCS-02 §3.4). The UPS output feeds the RTU (item
1), the cellular modem (item 4) and the enclosure heater (item 2)
4 Cellular modem and antenna on the approved carrier, SIM held by Alleniom Utilities
Alleniom (TCS-02 §4.1(c))
5 Communications entrance: 1 in conduit from the customer network Customer
room to the enclosure
6 Plant network drop: Cat 6 from customer switch SW-1 (plant LAN Customer
192.168.10.0/24) to RTU port 2
7 Recloser control link: RS-485 from the POI-R1 control cabinet to the Alleniom Utilities
RTU serial expansion card
3. UPS output loads
Load Draw Source of figure
RTU, Kelvraith YOT-8963 (item 1) 38 W typical Kelvraith YOT-8963 product data, 24
V DC supply module
Cellular modem (item 4) 12 W typical, continuous Approved-carrier modem data,
SCADA/EMS standard kit
Enclosure heater (item 2) 60 W, thermostat on Enclosure manufacturer data
below 5 degC
4. Notes
4.1 The RTU configuration (DNP3 addresses, point table, poll settings) is issued separately as
SCADA-PC-RTU-CFG-01 per TCS-02 §4.2; the plant-side devices it polls are listed in
SCADA-PC-RTU-DEV-01.
4.2 IP addressing on the plant side is assigned by Alleniom (TCS-02 §4.4); the customer's integrator, Ridgeway
Controls, supplied the device list.
4.3 Installation follows delivery and allocation of the RTU and POI recloser set under OG-17. This drawing does
not schedule the work.
Prepared: Marcus Deele, SCADA/EMS Engineer, 07/02/2025.